# A second `print` of a new expression at a stop outside the entry's file
# answers in under 100 ms on a program of 20,000 functions, as at a stop in
# the entry (second_print_answers_under_100ms.case). The stop is in lib.jet's
# `step`, which the entry prog.jet calls, so each print goes through the
# session's held check of the package's cut, which gains the functions of
# lib.jet it calls (DebugCompile.jet jet_cli_debug_eval_held_append), or
# compiles the package's sources cut to what it reaches
# (jet_cli_debug_eval_sliced), or goes through the held check of the program.
# Before, each print that called a program function
# fell back to compiling the program again: 2,290-2,420 ms per new
# expression at 20,000 functions (gate jet of 5f090c020d, stop in run).
# Both prints read `total`, 0 at the stop, and call the program's own
# functions: f_k(x) is (x + k) % 1000.
# gen/gen.jet writes lib.jet and prog.jet: step's first call, the stop, is
# lib.jet line 100003.
fixture: SecondPrintNonEntryUnder100ms.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet run gen/gen.jet -- 20000
exit: 0
stdout: = ""
session debug line: jet debug prog.jet
env: PATH={work}/no-tools
send debug: "break lib.jet:100003"
send debug: "c"
recv debug line until ~ "Breakpoint hit  lib.jet:100003  in step()" timeout 600s # the image builds and the program runs to the stop
send debug: "print f_1(total)"
recv debug line until ~ "f_1(total) = 1" timeout 600s # the first print
send debug: "print f_2(total) + f_3(total)"
recv debug line until ~ "f_2(total) + f_3(total) = 5" within 100ms # a second, new expression answers in under 100 ms
send debug: "c"
recv debug line until ~ "Program finished" timeout 600s # the evaluations left the program's run unchanged
close debug
exit: 0
